{
  "id": 250571188,
  "iid": 12065,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ftypes: Add functions to allocate with wmem",
  "description": "In proto.c, new_field_info allocates the field_info with\npinfo->pool scope. It contains a fvalue.\n\nIn cases where we hit an exception between new_field_info() and\nproto_tree_add_node(), we never end up calling proto_tree_free_node(),\nand hence fvalue_free() / fvalue_cleanup() don't get called to\nfree the fvalue.\n\nLet's allocate the fvalue_t there with the same wmem scope,\nensuring that it is automatically freed. Use a wmem callback\nto ensure that the value is freed as well.\n\nThis prevents leaking fvalue_t in proto.c on malformed packets.",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2023-09-13T11:59:05.794Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-09-15T11:54:42.372Z",
