        {
          "id": 1559169133,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "At least the only fvalues that get callbacks registered are bytes and strings, the ones with non-NULL free_value. I agree it's not ideal (replacing the strings and GByteArrays with wmem-allocated values is difficult in a way too.)\n\nIt could be possible to make `fvalue_free_wmem()` work for all allocators by storing the callback id, at the cost of increasing each fvalue_t in size.\n\nAt least the function is only used internally, and it's only used for pinfo->pool, which is the fast block allocator by default, which doesn't actually free anything anyway when `wmem_free()` is called (assuming that it's for a short lifetime, and thus it's better to free everything when the pool is destroyed or reset, which happens soon.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-14T13:20:18.074Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-15T08:41:30.569Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 250571188,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
