        {
          "id": 1560944964,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Right, the way it us being used is OKish, but the point is that the new API should not come with all these restrictions and trapdoors IMO.\n\nI do not think the callbacks were designed for this use case either. Otherwise why not use a hash table instead and delete callback entries in O(1)? And the key, I suppose could be the pointer itself, without having to save any IDs.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
