    {
      "id": "2d5ac29bf79ca4e2fc40e4845761be16b70bbf78",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1559308351,
          "type": null,
          "body": "What about this comment in the code:\n\n```\n\t/* Don't add new node to proto_tree until now so that any exceptions\n\t * raised by a tvbuff access method doesn't leave junk in the proto_tree. */\n\t/* XXX. wouldn't be better to add this item to tree, with some special flag (FI_EXCEPTION?)\n\t *      to know which item caused exception? */\n```\n\nMaybe add the item to the tree anyway, and use the flag to avoid displaying \"junk\" items? Not leaving it in the tree is what causes the leak in the first place.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
