    {
      "id": "36d0377c132af07ac96c63f50f7a503fd436f30d",
      "short_id": "36d0377c",
      "created_at": "2023-09-13T09:46:26.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "fb845cc4c483bbbbc2ebdc65998220cdd02aa7ee"
      ],
      "title": "ftypes: Add functions to allocate with wmem",
      "message": "ftypes: Add functions to allocate with wmem\n\nIn proto.c, new_field_info allocates the field_info with\npinfo->pool scope. It contains a fvalue.\n\nIn cases where we hit an exception between new_field_info() and\nproto_tree_add_node(), we never end up calling proto_tree_free_node(),\nand hence fvalue_free() / fvalue_cleanup() don't get called to\nfree the fvalue.\n\nLet's allocate the fvalue_t there with the same wmem scope,\nensuring that it is automatically freed. Use a wmem callback\nto ensure that the value is freed as well.\n\nThis prevents leaking fvalue_t in proto.c on malformed packets.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-09-12T19:01:12.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2023-09-13T09:46:26.000-04:00",
